      "expected": "C42 should match the 22nF value used by the other three capacitors in the corresponding network, unless the intentional difference is documented.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C42\") (value \"22pF 100v\") ... (description \" 100V 22nF X7R ...\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"CC0603KRX7R0BB223\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C44\") (value \"22nF 100v\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C45\") (value \"22nF 100v\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C46\") (value \"22nF 100v\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C42 VC4 Net-_C42-Pad2_ 22pF"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the schematic value is used for sourcing or assembly, this branch's capacitance is three orders of magnitude below the matching branches, changing the network's filtering and balance.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is supported by the netlist: both labeled CAN connectors are wired to both CAN bus pairs, contrary to the specified separate interfaces. C42 also has a 22pF schematic/SPICE value despite metadata and matching components indicating 22nF."
}

